===== GASTRIC SLEEVE DOC REVIEW =====
     1	Page: Gastric Sleeve Perth
     2	Verdict: Rework
     3	Reason: Safety, Medicare eligibility, hospital verification, cost certainty and outcome-claim issues need correction before publication.
     4	Counts: 8 must-fix · 12 should-fix · 4 minor
     5	Body word count: current body 1,844 words vs brief target 1,200-1,500 words, including FAQs.
     6	
     7	## Must fix before publish
     8	
     9	1. **AHPRA risk: the opening claim overstates safety and effectiveness**
    10	
    11	> Yet in the right hands, gastric sleeve surgery is a safe, powerful, and lasting weight loss tool.
    12	
    13	> For some people, gastric sleeve surgery can support substantial long-term weight loss, but it is major surgery with risks, and suitability needs to be assessed by a bariatric surgeon.
    14	
    15	Why it matters: "Safe, powerful, and lasting" creates an unbalanced beneficial expectation for a regulated health service, so risk balance needs to sit in the same sentence.
    16	
    17	2. **MBS/BMI eligibility is not accurate enough for Medicare item 31575 [also fix the brief]**
    18	
    19	> A sleeve gastrectomy is generally considered suitable for adults with a BMI of 35 or higher, or a BMI of 30-35 with associated weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnoea, or reflux.
    20	
    21	> For Medicare item 31575, MBS eligibility generally requires a BMI of 40 or higher, or a BMI of 35 or higher with a major comorbidity; eligibility is assessed individually by the surgeon and the relevant Medicare requirements should be confirmed.
    22	
    23	Why it matters: The draft's BMI 30-35 framing may be a broader clinical eligibility statement, but it should not sit unqualified on a page that also discusses Medicare item 31575; the writer followed the brief as instructed, so the brief also needs correction.
    24	
    25	3. **Hospital names must be verified with the client before changing either direction**
    26	
    27	> You'll spend 1-2 nights recuperating at [<u>Mount Private Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), or [<u>Waikiki Private Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/) in Perth.
    28	
    29	> Most patients spend around two nights in hospital at [the hospital location to be verified with the client], with discharge timing depending on recovery and clinical advice.
    30	
    31	Why it matters: The hospital names conflict with the brief, but the draft may reflect newer client information, so verify the correct hospital name(s) with the client before changing either direction.
    32	
    33	4. **The cost section needs consultation-based, no-dollar wording**
    34	
    35	> Draft L228-L246: **How much does a gastric sleeve cost in Perth?**
    36	>
    37	> Gastric sleeve surgery cost varies depending on your level of private health insurance cover, your surgeon and anaesthetist fees, hospital and theatre charges, and any out-of-pocket gap that applies to your situation. Medicare item number 31575 does attract a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component. Your surgeon’s fee for a primary laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy is \$4,000 for both insured and uninsured patients, rising to \$5,000 for a complex case. For those without private health cover, or where out-of-pocket costs are a concern, superannuation may be accessible as a funding option in certain circumstances, including: life-threatening conditions, certain psychiatric conditions, and the management of chronic pain. Financing options such as Zip and TLC are also available for eligible patients. A full breakdown of costs, funding pathways, and pre-surgical clinical fees can be found here.
    38	
    39	> Total out-of-pocket costs vary depending on private health cover, surgeon and anaesthetist fees, hospital charges, complexity and any applicable gap. Medicare item 31575 may attract a rebate when MBS requirements are met, while private health insurance may contribute to hospital and theatre costs depending on the policy, waiting periods and fund rules. Any current fee range should be discussed at consultation, together with the components that apply to your circumstances; ask the team to explain available funding pathways and review the current gastric sleeve cost guide before deciding whether to proceed.
    40	
    41	Why it matters: The brief explicitly says not to quote a single dollar figure. Costs, rebates, private-health benefits and funding pathways need current, approved disclosure and should be framed as matters to discuss at consultation.
    42	
    43	5. **Appetite and effectiveness wording are too certain**
    44	
    45	> Draft L57-L61: Gastric sleeve surgery is highly effective for weight loss for two key reasons: first, because your stomach is smaller, you feel fuller, faster. Secondly, because a reduced stomach size minimises your body’s production of ghrelin (the ‘hunger hormone’), after gastric sleeve surgery, your appetite will also be reduced.
    46	
    47	> The operation reduces stomach capacity, which may help some people feel full with smaller portions. It also removes part of the stomach that produces much of the body’s ghrelin, a hormone involved in hunger, so appetite changes vary between people in degree and duration.
    48	
    49	Why it matters: "Will also be reduced" reads like an outcome guarantee, while the rewrite keeps the mechanism and qualifies individual variation.
    50	
    51	6. **The "life-changing" phrase creates a transformational-benefit claim**
