   125	### Risks / honest section
   126	- **Intro paragraph tone:** Acknowledge directly that the bypass is a major operation and no surgery is without risk. Give the patient the full picture before deciding, including serious complications that can occur, and explain that the surgeon will discuss how each risk applies individually.
   127	- **Risk bullets to address:**
   128	  1. General surgical risks — bleeding, infection, blood clots, reaction to anaesthetic.
   129	  2. Small risk of a leak at one of the new surgical connections — monitored closely during the hospital stay.
   130	  3. Lifelong need for vitamin and mineral supplements, because the rerouting reduces nutrient absorption.
   131	  4. Dumping syndrome — feeling unwell after eating sugary or fatty foods; usually improves as eating habits adjust.
