105:> **4. How is a gastric sleeve different from a gastric bypass?** A gastric sleeve reduces stomach size without rerouting the small intestine. A gastric bypass reduces stomach size and reroutes part of the small intestine, so the procedures can have different nutritional and weight-loss effects. Reflux history, BMI, other health conditions and surgeon assessment all contribute to the choice; neither procedure is right for everyone.
