242:### G2 — MBS-inaccurate BMI wording
244:1. **The summary incorrectly places BMI 30-34 on a qualification pathway**
246:> Draft L84: As a general guide, surgical assessment is typically available for those with a BMI of ~35, and almost always from 40 and higher. Someone with a BMI of 30 to 34 may qualify where weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, or sleep apnoea are present and there have been previous attempts at weight loss through diet, exercise, or non-surgical means without lasting success. Please note that these are general clinical indicators only; your surgeon will make a clinical assessment and discuss your options with you when you meet.
248:> As a general guide, MBS eligibility is assessed individually. The relevant thresholds are BMI 40 or above, or BMI 35 or above with a major obesity-related comorbidity, alongside the applicable item, clinical and referral requirements. A BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold for these items; your surgeon will assess your wider health picture and discuss any other clinical pathways.
