262:> Draft L97-L100: BMI 35-39: most people in this range are eligible for a surgical assessment, with or without other health conditions. A range of procedures may be suitable, and your surgeon will discuss the options most appropriate for your situation.
264:> BMI 35-39: MBS eligibility is assessed individually. At BMI 35 or above, the MBS pathway requires a major obesity-related comorbidity alongside the applicable item, clinical and referral requirements. Your surgeon will assess your medical history, risks, goals and aftercare readiness before discussing options.
266:Why it matters: This is the known G2 error. BMI 35+ does not remove the major-comorbidity requirement for MBS eligibility.
